inferences.statement:
# 26. Important Research Integrity Constraint

We must not say:

> "BMC does not have dynamic arbitration."

The defensible statement is:

> **The reviewed public BMC documentation does not establish a generalized dynamic multi-option remediation arbitration capability.**

That is materially different.

A future investigation could still discover:

- native functionality;
- configuration patterns;
- custom-agent capabilities;
- customer implementations;
- partner solutions;
- product features not covered by the reviewed pages.

Therefore the opportunity remains open only as a research hypothesis.

---

