falsification.statement:
# 4. Multiple Options Do Not Prove Arbitration

This distinction is critical.

BMC exposing:

```text
A
B
C
```

does not prove that BMC dynamically decides:

```text
A > B > C
```

according to contextual trade-offs.

The reviewed documentation establishes policy matching and automation availability.

It does not establish a universal decision engine that scores competing remediation policies using:

- expected impact;
- risk;
- reversibility;
- blast radius;
- dependency state;
- current system health;
- downstream consequences;
- changing evidence.

# 26. Important Research Integrity Constraint

